Package: dracon-server
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: dracon-mod-staticcontent
Description: small, fast HTTP/HTTPS server for Linux
 Dracon is a small, fast HTTP/HTTPS server for Linux, written from scratch
 in C++23 on top of epoll and Boost.Coroutine2 (no Boost.Asio, no
 framework). The server itself only speaks HTTP: every request is
 answered by a plugin, a shared library loaded at start up. Each
 connection runs inside its own coroutine, so a handler is written as
 plain sequential code while every read and write that would block
 yields back to the event loop.
 .
 This package contains the server daemon, its systemd service, and the
 default configuration: it listens on port 80 out of the box (the systemd
 unit carries CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for that), with HTTPS on port 443
 configured but disabled since no certificate is shipped. It has no
 bundled content-serving plugin; install dracon-mod-staticcontent (or a
 plugin of your own) to actually answer requests.
 .
 Dracon is beta software: it has no stable plugin API/ABI yet.

Package: dracon-mod-staticcontent
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         dracon-server (= ${binary:Version})
Description: static file plugin for the Dracon HTTP server
 This plugin for the Dracon HTTP server (see dracon-server) serves plain
 files from the directories listed in static_files.conf, memory mapping
 them through an LRU cache. It also supports the traditional
 /~user/public_html mapping and per-path custom response headers.
 .
 The package also ships a default landing page in /usr/share/dracon/www,
 which is copied into the document root /var/www on installation if that
 directory does not exist yet or is still empty.
 .
 Dracon plugins have no stable ABI across versions, so this package is
 tied to an exact dracon-server build.

Package: libdracon-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         dracon-server (= ${binary:Version}),
         libboost-log-dev (>= 1.70)
Description: development files for Dracon plugins
 Dracon (see dracon-server) answers every HTTP request through a plugin: a
 shared library loaded with dlopen at start up. This package provides the
 header-only plugin API (requests and responses, streams and chunked
 output, RESTful routing, worker threads for slow work) and the CMake
 package config needed to build a plugin against an installed Dracon with
 find_package(Dracon).
 .
 Dracon is beta software: it has no stable plugin API/ABI yet, so a
 plugin built against one version is not guaranteed to load into another.

Package: python3-certbot-dracon
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-certbot
Recommends: dracon-server, dracon-mod-staticcontent
Description: Certbot plugin for the Dracon HTTP server
 A combined Certbot authenticator and installer for Dracon: it answers
 HTTP-01 challenges by dropping files where Dracon's staticContent plugin
 already serves "/", then installs the issued certificate into
 /etc/dracon, turns HTTPS on in server.conf, and restarts dracon.service.
 .
 Use it with:
 .
   certbot run --configurator dracon -d example.com
